  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Filter Kepler planet candidates by planet radius and host-star size and explore four charts, three coloured by a habitability class (promising/challenging/extreme), to find which planets and host stars look potentially habitable. The class comes from a fixed rule on planet temperature and planet radius (the README calls the radius test 'gravity'). The interface never shows the rule's thresholds. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
